   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 0.0,
   "duration": 9.873,
   "text": "Dijkstra's algorithm finds the shortest distance from one start node to every other node. The numbers on the edges are lengths. Every length must be zero or more.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "rule": 7.876
   },
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 7.867,
   "mark": "rule",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 9.867,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 9.867,
   "duration": 15.203,
   "text": "At the start, A has distance zero. Every other node has distance infinity. Then repeat two steps. First, settle the unsettled node with the smallest distance. Second, update its neighbors: if a path through it is shorter, keep the shorter distance.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "loop": 14.854
   },
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 14.85,
   "mark": "loop",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 25.067,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 25.067,
   "duration": 4.203,
   "text": "Settle A. From A, B is four away, and C is two away.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "r0": 26.161,
    "r1": 27.901
   },
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 26.15,
   "mark": "r0",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 27.9,
   "mark": "r1",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 29.267,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 29.267,
   "duration": 11.888,
   "text": "The smallest estimate is now C, at two. Settle C. Through C, B is two plus one: three. That is shorter than four, so B becomes three. D becomes ten, and E becomes twelve.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "r0": 33.092,
    "r1": 38.458,
    "r2": 39.73
   },
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
