  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 65.85,
   "duration": 3.166,
   "text": "Settle F, at thirteen. Every node is settled.",
   "bookmarks": {},
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 69.0,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 69.0,
   "duration": 12.22,
   "text": "Why is a settled distance final? Any other path must leave the settled nodes through an unsettled node, which is already at least as far. With no negative lengths, the rest of that path cannot make it shorter.",
   "bookmarks": {},
   "scene": "Dijkstra"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
